    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0042_a67f77c795aa.jpg\" style=\"width: 137px; height: 175px;\" /><br /><br />Chiral centers are four so 2<sup>4</sup> = 16 stereoisomers. Hence, 16 isomers are&nbsp; for glucose, and half of them will be for D-glucose and other half for L-glucose."
